   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Jobs and work",
     "texto": [
      "To say your job, you can use **Saya guru** (\"I'm a teacher\") or **Saya seorang guru** (\"I'm a person who teaches\"). Job names don't change for gender.",
      "**Kerja** means \"work\"; **bekerja**, \"to work\"; **pekerjaan**, \"job; occupation\". The prefix **ber-** forms a verb here. Unlike English \"works\", the verb doesn't change with the person: **saya bekerja** (\"I work\"), **dia bekerja** (\"he or she works\")."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Location and destination",
     "texto": [
      "**Di kantor** places someone \"in the office\". **Pergi ke kantor** shows that someone is going \"to the office\". In this use, **ke** shows the destination and **di** the place where someone is."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
